.through_sequence is an optional read guard; when absent, omit sequence arguments and use patch_page with block_id/expected_hash, or edit_page. Retain returned data for subsequent edits and inspect relevant fields; displaying an entire large envelope can truncate it. Successful reads use structuredContent without a duplicate MCP text copy. Optional references includes known MIME type and byte size for up to 128 links in returned Markdown; references_truncated signals more. Use inspect_page_reference for unknown metadata or read_page_reference for contents. With include_content=false, structuredContent.content is null. For meeting_notes Pages, follow meeting_context and read_page_transcript whenever the request depends on meeting context, including implicit requests. Existing native documents remain accessible when new creation is unavailable. This tool is part of plugin `Pages`.", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"block_ids": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}, "nullable": true, "description": "Optional nonempty array of 1..64 exact observed block IDs; duplicates are deduplicated. Omit or use null when unused, never []. Returns complete blocks in canonical order plus every instruction block. Missing IDs are reported with selection_complete=false. Mutually exclusive with search; requires editing view and include_content=true."}, "context_blocks": {"type": "number", "description": "Search only: preceding/following canonical blocks per match, 0..2; omitted means 1. Without search, omit this field even when its value would be 1. Positional context is not a semantic section. Selected results are limited to 128 blocks (complete or excerpted) and 256 KiB compact UTF-8 JSON including guidance; an explicit limit error replaces clipping. Use full view without selectors and filter locally when a complete block cannot fit."}, "context_lines": {"type": "number", "description": "Excerpts only: complete LF lines before/after every literal occurrence, 0..2